From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:24:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: map TERMINATE/INHIBIT_CHARGE to
 STATUS_FULL

qcom_fg_get_prop_batt_status() reads BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_1 and maps
TERMINATE_CHARGE and INHIBIT_CHARGE -- the states the charger state
machine enters once the battery reaches float voltage and charging
stops -- to POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING. With a charger permanently
attached this makes GNOME (and anything else reading
power_supply_class) show "Charging" forever once the battery is
actually full and topped off.

qcom_smbx.c reads the identical BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_1 register on
the same PMI8998 hardware block (same register offset 0x06, same
TRICKLE/PRE/FAST/FULLON/TAPER/TERMINATE/INHIBIT/DISABLE enum), and
already maps both states to POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL. Do the same
here so the fuel gauge and the charger driver agree on what "full"
means for the same battery.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
index 5fa1f0b0f7d9..16d8a2fe407e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -604,9 +604,11 @@ int qcom_fg_get_prop_batt_status(struct qcom_fg_chip *chip, int *val)
 	case FAST_CHARGE:
 	case FULLON_CHARGE:
 	case TAPER_CHARGE:
+		*val = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+		break;
 	case TERMINATE_CHARGE:
 	case INHIBIT_CHARGE:
-		*val = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+		*val = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 		break;
 	case DISABLE_CHARGE:
 		*val = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
